;
RUNNING THE BULLETIN BOARD

A - Sysop access
B - Looking after your board
:A
SYSOP ACCESS

RBBS is the board's public entry command. It supports discussion
forums and private mail between registered callers.

Use private local CP/M for sysop business. The initial credentials
are in the private host file SYSOP.DOC. Never enter them on a shared
console. Use the board's supplied maintenance menus.

A15: contains board programs and static files. I15: contains the
accounts and message base. The public RBBS launcher has a controlled
exception for these areas; callers need no direct access to them.
:B
LOOKING AFTER YOUR BOARD

A few active forums are better than a dozen empty ones.
Choose subjects that suit your callers and post a welcome message
explaining the purpose of each forum. Check new accounts and keep
an eye on the message base.

Do not promise absolute confidentiality for private mail. The sysop
controls the disks and backups; raw TCP is unencrypted.

Back up the complete stopped installation before major changes.
Exact maintenance menus can differ between board revisions; follow
the instructions displayed by your installed RBBS.
